  "notes": "Pencil page 13, no manuscript page number. This page continues “Par construction, tout completed-C_0-morphisme” from scan 012, rather than the unfinished sentence on scan 013. It gives (18)–(22), the factorization through a C_0-morphism and a completed isomorphism, a uniqueness criterion, and a composition recipe. The upper marginal note asserts conservativity and describes completed isomorphisms. It writes a hatted f_0 even in the test for a C_0-isomorphism; the hat is retained. The lower marginal note warns “Il faut savoir interpréter ... déjà la relation” as membership in the completed stabilizer. Its product group is visibly Aut(X)×Aut(Y), although for the displayed u:Y′→Y the first factor would be Aut(Y′); the clear X is retained. The diagram’s two lifts carry literal question marks. The final algebraic rearrangement checks once phi-hat u=u psi-hat is supplied; this calculation does not by itself establish the stabilizer-completion identification. The apparent prefix on morphisme comes from the slanted marginal formula overlapping that line, not an epi prefix.",
